\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Probability pushforwards require a positive source}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The probability theorem \ref{fdip-00G8} requires a
reflection-positive source measure and a measurable map
intertwining reflections. Pullback must preserve positive-half
observables; on finite configuration spaces, it is the
algebra map of \ref{fdip-00XI}.}

\p{A Berezin coefficient is a signed linear functional.
The probability theorem still requires a reflection-positive
source measure. Algebraic restriction by \ref{fdip-00XI}
requires multiplicativity and half-preservation; idempotence
alone gives neither property to a linear projector combining
both halves.}
